[Music]  hey what's up guys I'm Kay PhD here and  this is the Chromebook pixel and it's my  unboxing and first impressions now  before you guys go all whoa mkbhd you  must be nuts for paying $1,300 for a web  browser take a second go ahead and check  out my Chromebook pixel explaining video  it opens in a new tab it's the first  link below the like button on this video  and that'll take you to my first  impressions and thoughts on this machine  but now I have it here in person to  check it out for myself and hopefully  I'll be able to give you guys enough  information from my experience with it  to help you decide what you think of the  pixel either way let's get into this  full retail unboxing since I wasn't one  of the cool kids to get a loaner from  Google right off the bat when you open  the box you're presented with the  Chromebook itself super nice and I also  like this packaging but we'll put that  to the side for a second next you  actually get a card with some help so  there's a site dedicated to Chromebook  pixel customer support so that's cool  then of course below that is the charger  it's very reminiscent of the Asus  Zenbook and MacBook chargers that plug  directly into the wall so it's a pretty  small brick and it does say Chrome on it  which is a nice touch then again you  also get the larger cable so if you want  to plug it into the wall further away  from you that is totally cool too and  then you get your safety and warranty  information as well and that's it the  unboxing is done so taking a closer look  at the laptop it is immediately apparent  as soon as you pick it up and hold the  thing that it is built well it is a  completely unibody design and it's a  really nice clean feel no obtrusive  logos or anything protruding anywhere in  fact it's one of the most minimalist  understated designs you could say  handsome designs of any laptop I've ever  seen including the original cr-48  Chromebook this port layout is also as  we have expected pretty basic on the  left side there's power a mini display  port two USB 2.0 ports and an audio port  and on the right side is just an SD card  reader so although this is all nice and  pretty basic I would have liked to see  more video out options like some HDMI  action thrown in there but that's  alright all this looking around the  device also really gets you to look at  two things one how thin it really is on  to how much attention to detail went  into this design it's a really handsome  notebook it's nice and clean  unibody feel like I said everything from  the hinge to the logo placement if you  in the right place and I love that and  then you open it up for the first time  and Chrome OS boots and the display  turns on and then you realize why this  thing is premium that is a 2560 by 1713  inch display and it has a pixel density  of 239 PPI this is the sharpest display  we've ever seen in a laptop and don't  worry yes I will go more into the detail  with that in the full review video but  basically the display is awesome in  every way I've watched the Timescape 4k  demo video that comes pre-loaded on it  just for kicks and you can see  everything every little detail it really  does show up as being a little bit  glossy though so you'll have to angle it  properly to get rid of the lights but  then again it is a touchscreen too so  there is some fun thrown into there I  don't know it's just an awesome package  centered around that nice display which  is where the Chromebook pixel gets its  name so the hardware is pretty much at  first glance definitely awesome and  playing around with Chrome OS version 25  is also fun too now most of us are  already familiar with Chrome most of us  in fact are probably watching this video  in chrome right now but Chrome OS has a  lot of additions and tweaks to it that  make it seem like way more than just a  browser first of all all the multi  window support is nice the search  functionality all the keys that are  integrated with it and the inevitable  upcoming additions like Google now and  notifications etc all these things  hopefully will come together to make  this feel like a more complete operating  system experience plus the touch screens  so that really gives you sort of a new  experience with Google Chrome now it's  difficult to live completely in the  cloud for some people and I understand  that but the purpose of this video right  here the reason this video is on YouTube  is to ask you guys what do you want to  see in the Chromebook pixel full review  the comments section below is wide open  right below that like button and it'll  serve as a forum for all your  suggestions do you want to see  performance tests you know more info on  the screen on the operating system  gaming whatever it is let me know and I  will see it also without giving away too  much I do plan on comparing this to the  competition but that's a whole nother  mother of a topic altogether so anyway  let me know guys I'll leave you with the  Konami Easter Egg that  with that awesome badass light bar that  Google added just for kicks because it  looks cool there you go thank you for  watching and I'll talk to you guys in  the next one peace  [Music]  you  [Music]

